    architecture: '```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  P[Producer] --> CI[CI compatibility check - BACKWARD mode]\n  CI -->|pass| REG[(Schema registry - subject + version)]\n  CI -->|breaking| BLK[PR fails - migrate or dual-publish]\n  REG --> APP[Consumers pinned to version]\n  CT[Contract tests replay real messages] --> CI\n```\n\n**Key components:**\n- Registry: compatibility mode checked per subject at publish time, never at runtime\n- CI gate: a breaking candidate never ships — dual-field migration is the escape hatch\n- Contract tests: consumer-driven replay of production messages against the candidate schema',
    tradeoffs: '| Decision | Chosen | Alternative | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Compatibility | BACKWARD default | FULL everywhere | Consumers upgrade on their schedule |\n| Format | Avro/Protobuf + registry | Raw JSON | Typed schemas make breaks mechanically detectable |\n| Migration | Expand/contract | Big-bang | Rolling deploys need both shapes live',
    approach: '**How to structure 30 min:** classify the change (additive vs breaking) → enforcement points (registry, CI, review) → storage migration path → consumer comms.',
    followUp: '**Follow-up:** Zero-downtime column-type migration?\n> Expand/contract: add new column, dual-write, backfill, switch readers, drop old.',
    pitfalls: '- No publish-time compatibility enforcement\n- Nobody runs consumer contract tests'
